grq(){return"ironvibe.app"},
grp(){return"Privacy policy"},
grN(){return"GUIDE"},
guC(){return"How it works"},
gtu(){return'IronVibe deliberately ships without a built-in exercise catalog or preset "programs." It is not here to teach you how to train\u2014YouTube and real coaches already do that\u2014but to help you keep stats exactly the way you like. You type exercise names yourself, in your own words. Optionally tag a muscle group so the app can assemble a quick full-body session from your own list. The longer you use it, the more it feels like home: the app learns your habits and adapts to you, not the other way around.'},
gud(){return"Set controls"},
gp8(){return"Minus"},
gug(){return"Removes the last set. If that row already has weight, reps, or RIR, the app asks for confirmation. An empty row is removed right away. If only one set remains: in the current workout the row is cleared; in saved history the whole exercise is deleted."},
gp9(){return"Plus"},
guh(){return"Adds a new empty set row to this exercise."},
gpa(){return"Timeline"},
gui(){return"Opens the progress timeline for this exercise."},
gu9(){return"Progress chart"},
gtz(){return"Three independent trends by date: red \u2014 heaviest single set that day; cyan \u2014 most reps in any single set that day; yellow \u2014 exercise volume (sum of weight \xd7 reps for that day). Left axis: weight; right axis: reps; yellow is shown as a normalized trend."},
gtD(){return"Red line: maximum weight in one set on each calendar day."},
gtB(){return"Cyan line: maximum reps in one set that day (not tied to the heaviest weight)."},
gtC(){return"Yellow line: daily exercise volume (tonnage), calculated as the sum of weight \xd7 reps for sets where both values are logged."},
gtA(){return"During an active workout, the chart button under the sets may tint in the same colors as the graph: red if you beat your previous best weight in a single set; yellow if total exercise volume beats your past best for that movement; cyan if the exercise is bodyweight-only and your total reps (sum across all sets) beat your past best. If several apply, priority is red, then yellow, then cyan. The tint appears only while you are logging the current workout\u2014not in saved history."},
guf(){return"Workout"},
grI(){return"Add exercise"},
grH(){return"Adds a new block. Name the current exercise first \u2014 the app will remind you if that field is still empty."},
gu3(){return"Exercise name"},
gtP(){return"Long press to rename"},
gtO(){return"Long-press the exercise name while logging a workout, on a suggestion in the dropdown, or on the title in a saved workout in history to rename that exercise everywhere."},
gtN(){return"Remove from your list"},
gtM(){return"When the suggestions list is open under the name field, tap the X on a row \u2014 or the red X in Personal Progress \u2014 to remove that name from suggestions and the progress table. Saved workouts stay unchanged."},
gu6(){return"Data fields"},
guN(){return"Weight"},
guM(){return"Load on the bar or equipment. Type the number in kg or lb \u2014 whichever you use. The app does not convert units."},
gtR(){return"Reps"},
